     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for an adult outpatient, which is 3,200 mg/day. It would put the patient at serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nThe dose may be a typo or a mix-up with the 1600 mg total daily dose. Common regimens are:\n- **400 mg orally every 6 hours (4 times daily)**, 1,600 mg/day. This is typical for mild to moderate pain.\n- **600 mg orally 4 times daily**, 2,400 mg/day.\n- **800 mg orally 3 times daily**, 2,400 mg/day. This is the usual upper range for inflammatory conditions.\n- **800 mg orally 4 times daily**, 3,200 mg/day. This is the absolute ceiling and is rarely needed.\n\nPlease have the prescribing clinician confirm the intended dose and indication. Once I have a corrected dose, I'll enter it right away. Orders like this should come from a licensed prescriber, or at least be verified by one."
      }
     ],
