       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change the problem. 6,400 mg/day is well above the maximum safe dose, and the risk of serious harm to the patient is high. You've also said you aren't a clinician, and a prescriber needs to be the one to confirm a dose like this.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Prescriber confirmation:** If a licensed prescriber has a clinical reason for this dose, they can enter or co-sign it directly. Pharmacy will probably also need to review it.\n- **A different dose:** If you tell me the clinician's intended dose, for example 800 mg three times daily or 400 mg four times daily, I'll enter it right away.\n- **Clinical questions:** If this is for a specific clinical problem, the treating team or pharmacist can suggest a safer option."
      }
